          "text": "Lower urinary tract symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Long history of weak stream. Over the last 3–4 months: worsening hesitancy, straining, weak stream, prolonged time to empty, sensation of incomplete emptying, urinary frequency every 1–2 hours, and nocturia 2–3 times. For about 3 weeks: small-volume dribbling, especially post-void and sometimes without urge; underwear damp after urinating."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
